<title>UK: EU sells 52,460 T German intvn rye at 94.58 Ecus.</title>
<headline>EU sells 52,460 T German intvn rye at 94.58 Ecus.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The EU grains management committee on Thursday sold 52,460 tonnes of German intervention rye at a minimum price of 94.58 Ecus per tonne for export to non-EU countries, member state officials said.</p>
<p>There were no other intervention awards, the officials said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
